        <description><![CDATA[<p>If an employee has reasonable cause to believe that a danger exists and wants to exercise their right to refuse dangerous work, the employee must first remove themselves from the situation and then complete the form below.</p>
<p>This form is used to submit a refusal to work in accordance with the definition of danger in the <a href="https://hoccdc.sharepoint.com/sites/info/en/services/hoc-health-and-wellness/Documents/Right-to-refuse-dangerous-work-procedure-e.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">HoC right-to-refuse-dangerous-work-procedure-e.pdf</a>. An employee may refuse to use or operate a machine or thing, to work in a place, or to perform an activity if the employee, while at work, has reasonable cause to believe that:</p>
<ul style="list-style-position: inside;"><li>the use or operation of the machine or thing constitutes a danger to the employee or to another employee;</li><li>a condition exists in the place that constitutes a danger to the employee;<br />or</li><li>the performance of the activity constitutes a danger to the employee or to another employee.</li></ul>
<p>For post exposure to a chemical or information pertaining to a chemical product, you may refer to the <a title="SDS Repository" href="https://webhouseofcommons77ff9fjquf.maerixium.com/paratoxxpress/binder/default/EN/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">SDS Repository</a> for further information.</p>]]></description>
